       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg once daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **Dosing error.** If you meant 100 mg or 200 mg daily, tell me the dose. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg once daily, and the usual start is 25\u201350 mg.\n2. **Intentional.** If you really want 600 mg, for example under a specialist protocol, confirm that and give me the indication. I'll enter it with a note that the dose is above the labeled maximum and was confirmed by you. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **Different drug or unit.** If you meant another medication, or 60 mg, tell me.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
